+## Current voyage
+
+**Acceptance-suite failures (real browser Cypress, fixed test, 10 failures):**
+
+| Group | Failure | Root cause | Fix required |
+|-------|---------|------------|--------------|
+| A (tests 1-4) | DOM detachment on toggle/toggle-all | `render()` replaces all `<li>` via `innerHTML = ''`; browser references to previous nodes become detached | Mutate existing DOM in place — toggle `.completed` class and `.checked` on existing nodes instead of rebuilding list |
+| B (tests 5-10) | Edit input not visible / label not hidden | dblclick handler sets `todo.editing = true` in memory then calls `render()` which reloads `todos` from localStorage (via `getTodos()`). `setTodos()` strips `editing` flag before save, so `editing` class NEVER applied; edit input stays `display: none` | Preserve `editing` through render: either pass transient state explicitly, or set `editing` directly on DOM without re-rendering |
+
+**Scenarios that will fail with honest step definitions:**
+- `Edit input is visible when entering edit mode` — QM creates step using `getComputedStyle`, fails because `editing` class never applied → `display: none`
+- `View controls are hidden when editing` — QM creates step using `getComputedStyle`, fails because `.view` never gets `display: none`
+
+**Perturbation needed in watchbill:** `render()` seam (`js/app.js`) for DOM-identity defect (browser-only, harness cannot reproduce).
+
 ## Decisions
 
 - Storage key: `todos-vanillajs` per spec convention (`todos-[framework]`).
-- Tier: happy-dom (default). The spec requires DOM rendering; happy-dom is the cheapest tier that observes it.
+- Tier: happy-dom (default).
 - Scantling for localStorage shape at `scantlings/todo-storage.json`.
+- Fixed acceptance suite (Cypress, real browser) is authoritative; harness workarounds in step definitions mask bugs.
+- Editing visibility scenarios use step concepts QM must implement with computed-style checks.
 
